title: Tell better from different by probes written before the tending, answered by fresh minds from the graph as it was and as it is.
pid: b1f43a56-8686-49c0-a204-0c4fbee54078
body: |2-
  A tending is better if a mind holding only the graph answers more of
  what that specialist's next missions will need, loses nothing it
  answered before, and reads no more to do it. Probes, not judgment:
  a mind asked whether a graph is better judges the writing, and the
  writing is what changed. Every published measure is of this kind,
  the task done with the memory before and after and with none at all
  (ACE, the faulty-memory paper, MemoryAgentBench), never a rating of
  the memory itself. It is how [[id:034344fc-388e-4248-ac3b-d130d1049568][Tay's note on Jeff's taste was tested]]:
  cases with known answers, minds holding only the note.
  Git already holds ten such pairs from 2026-11-13, a commit "as NAME
  left it" followed by "Tended: ...", in Vic's, Tay's, Cleo's, Libby's
  and Drew's skgrepos, so the test can be run on tendings already done
  before any more are. The steps are in [[id:acc8c677-9169-43ab-9bc2-e14c190d6442][the probe test of a tending, step by step]].
